WEBVTT

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:18.600
Do you hear?  Hooves beating

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:30.750
A carriage goes through the gentle hills

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:37.980
Someone comes to pick me up

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:45.950
And takes me

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.900
To the avenue with white flowers

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:58.050
To the home of wind

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.400
He takes me

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.900
I'm sure

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:34.940
Good morning, Anne!

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.130
Good morning.

00:01:37.470 --> 00:01:39.810
What's wrong? You don't look very well.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:51.130
The river is singing happily
and the flowers are smiling to the sky.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:55.500
Spring has come.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:02.820
You must be tired from the extra lessons
for Queens. Let's talk about something fun.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.790
Queens? Maybe you're right.

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:37.900
Spring had come again to Green Gables

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:40.990
and all the world was abloom once more.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:45.690
The season has a
negative affect in the student's.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:55.390
While the others scattered to green lanes
and leafy wood cuts and meadow byways,

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:59.720
the Queen's class, left behind in school,
looked wistfully out of the windows.

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:04.890
The winter passed away in a
round of pleasant duties and studies,

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:08.220
but now, the enthusiasm
was slowly ebbing away.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:13.630
Even Anne and Gilbert lagged
and grew indifferent.

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:18.470
And then, Anne heard some shocking news.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:22.800
Is it true that Miss Stacy is
not coming back the next year, Anne?

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:23.980
How can that be!?

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:25.280
I didn't know anything.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:30.440
I heard that she had been offered a position
in the grade school of her own home district.

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:34.220
And that the teacher meant to accept.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:37.600
But... then what will
become of the Queen's lessons?

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:39.000
I wonder...

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.780
I won't believe that rumor.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.860
She has always put
her heart into educating us.

00:03:44.860 --> 00:03:49.630
But I heard it from Mrs. Lynde.
And she's a school council member.

00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:59.110
What are we going to do?
I don't think I'll be able to get into Queens.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:01.840
But we don't even know if it's true.

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.190
Let's just go ask her directly.

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:05.980
I don't have the courage.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:07.740
That's right.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:11.810
If she answers that
she really is planing to leave,

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:14.270
I would be really disappointed.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:15.410
Miss Stacy is coming.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.190
What's wrong?

00:04:20.190 --> 00:04:22.240
You should be
happy that vacation is coming.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.640
Just be a little more patience.

00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:26.940
Come on, cheer up.
Let's continue the class.

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:45.050
For how long does she intends to sleep?

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:47.040
Well now...

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:52.230
She should be getting up soon.

00:04:52.230 --> 00:04:57.220
Lately she gets up so late that she doesn't
even have time for breakfast.

00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:00.580
She doesn't even have time
to complete her tasks.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:05.570
Before she used to worry about her studies
and helped much more around the house.

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:09.780
Well now... Maybe she's tired.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.610
Anne?

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:17.960
But she's still the same during the day
and talks just as much.

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:22.190
But with her studies she doesn't
even have time to play.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:27.580
Yes, maybe you're right.

00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:31.320
But it's hard to believe the she could get tired.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:36.800
Anne, you are going to
be late if you don't wake up soon!

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:39.020
Anne! Anne!

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.420
Yes...

00:05:56.980 --> 00:06:00.820
The last day of the school term has arrived.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:04.300
Well, this was the last Queen's class of the year.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:10.640
All of you seem a little tired, and
to say the truth I'm a little relieved.

00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:15.780
But you've worked well this past year.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:19.210
And you deserve a good, jolly vacation.

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:24.130
Have the best time you can in the out-of-door
world and lay in a good stock of health

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:27.440
and vitality and ambition
to carry you through next year.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:29.640
It will be the tug of war,

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:32.360
the last year before the Entrance.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:37.580
This is strange...

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:39.230
What's wrong, everyone?

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.220
You're all so quiet.

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:42.990
Miss Stacy!

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:46.070
Are you going to be back next year?

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:49.490
So it's because of that?

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.580
Yes, I think I will.

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:07.400
They offered me the
chance to teach at the school
where I studied and I was thinking about it,

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:10.750
but I have decided to come back to Avonlea.

00:07:11.010 --> 00:07:17.190
I've grown so interested in you all.
So I'll stay and see you through.

00:07:17.190 --> 00:07:18.460
Hurrah!

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:27.550
Thank you, Miss Stacy!

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:28.580
Thank you!

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:29.240
I'm so relieved!

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:30.800
Don't be silly.

00:07:31.290 --> 00:07:35.460
It would be perfectly
dreadful if you didn't come back.

00:07:36.240 --> 00:07:40.380
I don't believe I could have the heart to go on
with my studies if another teacher came here.

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:41.430
That's true!

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:43.610
Oh, that would be a problem.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:47.330
But you should be
here for yourselves, and not for me.

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:50.300
So no matter what happens,
you should study hard.

00:07:50.540 --> 00:07:51.280
Of course.

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:55.130
We know that.
But we're really relieved.

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:59.400
Hey, Charlie, now you can rest assured.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.850
Yes, and the same goes to you.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:06.780
Well, everyone, we'll meet again
in two months' time.

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.090
Yes!

00:08:13.250 --> 00:08:14.640
Matthew, I'm home!

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:17.030
My vacations start tomorrow!

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:19.140
The school term ended today.

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:20.340
Is that so?

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:21.650
Do you want a ride?

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:22.540
Yes.

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:41.330
I'm home, Marilla!

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:44.160
My vacations start tomorrow!

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:50.330
My my, the child loves to study,
but she must be really tired of it.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:28.270
What are you doing here?

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:30.400
You didn't even washed the bottle.

00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:31.860
Oh Marilla!

00:09:31.860 --> 00:09:36.790
I'm packing my schoolbooks because I don't
want to see them during my vacations.

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:40.980
I've studied as hard all the term as possibly

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:44.580
and I've studied geometry until I knew
everything in the first book.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:46.920
I just feel tired of everything sensible

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:50.360
and I'm going to let my imagination
run riot for the summer.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:51.870
Don't joke with me.

00:09:51.870 --> 00:09:57.220
You know what it happens when you let
your imagination run wild, don't you?

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:59.640
Oh, you needn't be alarmed, Marilla.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.530
I'll only let it run riot within
reasonable limits.

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:07.280
I wonder. In any case I'm worried about
such long vacations.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:12.470
Please don't climb up onto
Mr. Barry's roof again this year.

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:23.350
But I want to have a real good jolly time
this summer, Matthew.

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:28.850
For maybe it's the
last summer I'll be a little girl.

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:33.260
Well, you really are growing up fast.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:35.430
Mrs. Lynde says that

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:38.520
if I keep stretching out, next year
I'll have to put on longer skirts.

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:40.780
And that I'm all running to legs and eyes.

00:10:41.060 --> 00:10:43.640
It was terrible of her to say such things.

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:45.250
You're right.

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:50.170
When I put on longer skirts I shall feel that I
have to live up to them and be very dignified.

00:10:50.450 --> 00:10:52.410
It will be strange if
I still behave like a child, right?

00:10:52.990 --> 00:10:56.550
It won't even do to
believe in fairies then, I'm afraid.

00:10:56.870 --> 00:11:01.350
So I'm going to believe in them
with all my whole heart this summer.

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:05.010
I think we're going
to have a very nice vacation.

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:09.040
Ruby Gillis is going to
have a birthday party soon

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:11.370
and there's the Sunday
school picnic next month.

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:14.930
And the missionary concert.

00:11:14.930 --> 00:11:16.760
And also... Well...

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:22.050
That's very nice, but don't you think
you should study at least a little?

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:24.250
I've already told you.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:28.140
I won't touch any schoolbook
for these two months.

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:32.100
Schoolbooks won't
help me with my imagination.

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:34.720
I hope that you're not pretending to
use your vacations

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:38.270
to imagine all the time instead
of helping around the house.

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:40.120
No, don't worry.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:44.110
Since I'm a grown up
I will do everything I must do.

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:46.250
Well, well, that's a relief.

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:48.570
Lately you've been very lazy.

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:49.900
I'm sorry.

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:53.470
I can't seem to get
up early during Springtime.

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:54.470
Yes.

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:58.720
You are probably very
tired due to the load of schoolwork.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.990
That is why...

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:03.130
You think that I'm tired?

00:12:04.120 --> 00:12:04.880
That can't be.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:06.560
I'm alright, Matthew.

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:08.020
I'm not tired.

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:10.420
I'm full of energy.

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:13.360
Oh, my vacations start tomorrow.

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:25.680
On the next day, after breakfast,

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:28.450
Anne went to see Diana.

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:34.490
They were going to discuss how to
spend the next two months.

00:12:34.680 --> 00:12:36.330
Good morning, Diana!

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:46.190
And on that afternoon...

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:53.660
I'm going to the Aid meeting now.

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.340
I asked Anne to make the tea.

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:58.460
So she must be home soon.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:00.790
Alright. I'll see you later.

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:09.660
M-Matthew!

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:12.320
Are you alright, Matthew!?

00:13:15.400 --> 00:13:17.240
Jerry Buote! Jerry!

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:18.420
Come here!

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:32.670
Matthew's heart
hasn't been well for a while.

00:13:33.720 --> 00:13:36.600
That was why they wanted a boy
from the orphanage to help him.

00:13:36.600 --> 00:13:42.250
They wanted to lessen his workload.

00:13:43.740 --> 00:13:46.580
His life doesn't seem to be in danger for now.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:51.510
I already told you that you
shouldn't do any heavy work.

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:54.190
And you must be careful to avoid excitement.

00:13:54.480 --> 00:13:55.690
Well now...

00:13:56.320 --> 00:14:01.200
But I can't just stop working, Doctor.

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:03.140
Is that so?

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:05.730
But we can't be too careless.

00:14:05.880 --> 00:14:08.720
However it doesn't help if
you keep worrying about it.

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:13.630
Please, call me if anything happens again.

00:14:13.980 --> 00:14:15.670
Thank you very much.

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:19.840
Remember, don't work so much
and be careful to avoid excitement.

00:14:20.300 --> 00:14:22.180
I understand, Doctor.

00:14:22.810 --> 00:14:26.050
I'm sorry to make
you come all the way here.

00:14:31.490 --> 00:14:33.320
Where is Anne Shirley?

00:14:33.330 --> 00:14:35.780
Anne? She got out to play.

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:37.310
Is anything wrong with her?

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:41.640
No. It's just that I saw her not to
long ago, and she seemed a little pale.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:46.590
She seems different from
last year when she broke her leg.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:49.540
Don't tell me that she's ill?

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:53.000
No, no. I don't think so.

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:57.120
But I think fresh
air would be good for her.

00:14:57.230 --> 00:15:00.640
Let her have some
fun during her vacations.

00:15:02.150 --> 00:15:04.100
I heard she's an excellent student.

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:09.760
But if she continues to neglect her
health, she might get some lung disease.

00:15:09.840 --> 00:15:10.860
L-Lung disease?

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:12.830
She has lung disease?

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:14.710
Please calm down.

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:18.420
I didn't want to alarm you.
It was just a warning.

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:25.070
I see. I thought that was strange that
lately she doesn't want to get out of bed.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.910
There's nothing to be worried about.

00:15:28.410 --> 00:15:33.200
Just let her enjoy herself during her
vacation, and everything will be alright.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.380
I'll be back when
you need me. Goodbye.

00:15:56.310 --> 00:16:00.620
I told her not to exert herself too much
for the Queens Classes.

00:16:03.020 --> 00:16:05.990
That child studies too much.

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:10.900
But then again she gets too
passionate about everything.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:15.250
What if she really gets sick?

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:29.420
That it's strange.

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:34.140
She really knew that she needed to have fun.

00:16:34.510 --> 00:16:38.090
For some time, the only
thing she cared was her studies.

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:45.150
You shouldn't be out of bed.

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:46.550
You have got to rest.

00:16:46.830 --> 00:16:50.830
No, I'm alright.
It's not the first time this happens.

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:55.150
I just need to rest a little.

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:58.720
There was no need to call the Doctor.

00:16:59.280 --> 00:17:01.720
But you have to listen
to the Doctor this time.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:04.470
Let Jerry do all the heavy work.

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:05.530
You are...

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:12.220
I understood. By the way, did the Doctor
mention something about Anne just now?

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:17.390
Yes, he said that he saw Anne the other
day and noticed that she has grown taller,

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:21.860
and also that he heard she's an
excellent student. All good things.

00:17:23.370 --> 00:17:25.180
Well now, Marilla

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:32.760
don't tell anything to Anne
about my ailment, like we did till now.

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:33.960
If we did...

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:36.470
I knew you would say that.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:38.700
Yes, I won't tell her, Matthew.

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:43.100
And you shouldn't be worrying like that.
It's not good for your heart.

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:45.290
Well, I'll get you some tea.

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:51.290
It's a good thing that Anne is not around.

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:56.600
Or she would want
to help Matthew with his work.

00:18:06.380 --> 00:18:08.170
Oh, Matthew, you already here?

00:18:08.490 --> 00:18:09.770
I'll go make you some tea.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:11.830
W-Well now...

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:16.050
Marilla?
What about the Aid meeting?

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:19.150
I had a little headache.
So I didn't go today.

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:22.180
Really?
I'm sorry, I'm late.

00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:26.110
It's alright.
By the way, did you have fun today?

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:30.780
Well, I spent the day at
Diana's house talking like a lady.

00:18:30.990 --> 00:18:35.760
We haven't had such a good
chat since I joined the Queens Class.

00:18:36.010 --> 00:18:38.730
That won't do.
You have to spend more time outside.

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:43.690
Didn't you say you
were going to have a lot of fun?

00:20:22.480 --> 00:20:23.750
In the next afternoon,

00:20:24.470 --> 00:20:28.430
after Diana and
Anne spent the day together,

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:33.050
Mrs. Lynde went to Green Gables.

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:39.060
She wanted to find out why Marilla had not
been at the Aid meeting yesterday.

00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:42.590
Matthew had a bad spell
with his heart yesterday.

00:20:42.590 --> 00:20:45.920
Oh my, again?
That's not a good sign!

00:20:46.230 --> 00:20:49.700
And I didn't feel like leaving him.

00:20:49.700 --> 00:20:52.720
He's all right again now

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:56.930
but he takes them spells oftener than
he used to and I'm anxious about him.

00:20:57.740 --> 00:21:02.320
The doctor says he must
be careful to avoid excitement.

00:21:02.750 --> 00:21:05.550
Well, that's easy enough.

00:21:06.000 --> 00:21:10.490
For Matthew doesn't go about looking for
excitement by any means and never did.

00:21:10.720 --> 00:21:11.550
You're right.

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:14.790
But he's not to do
any very heavy work either

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:19.670
and you might as well tell Matthew
not to breathe as not to work.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:20.830
That's true.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:23.900
Rachel. You'll stay to tea?

00:21:24.200 --> 00:21:29.290
Anne is going to make some cookies today.
You have to try some.

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:30.880
Anne?

00:21:31.280 --> 00:21:33.920
Then I will have to try them.

00:21:35.250 --> 00:21:38.340
Speaking of Anne, here she comes.

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:41.020
Good afternoon, Mrs. Lynde.

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:43.830
Today I arrived on time.

00:21:43.830 --> 00:21:45.200
Look, I brought a gift.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:46.420
Aren't they pretty?

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:50.740
I'll make the cookies right away.

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:56.950
She doesn't know anything
about Matthew's illness.

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:02.790
While Marilla was
speaking with Mrs. Lynde,

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:05.770
Anne made tea and baked cookies.

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:11.790
And even the critical Mrs. Lynde couldn't
find anything wrong in the cookies.

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:16.110
These cookies are really delicious!

00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:19.450
I was finally praised by Mrs. Lynde.

00:22:24.290 --> 00:22:27.140
I must say Anne has
turned out a real smart girl.

00:22:27.460 --> 00:22:29.280
She must be a great help to you.

00:22:29.900 --> 00:22:34.530
She is. I used to be afraid she'd
never get over her featherbrained ways,

00:22:34.800 --> 00:22:37.570
but she has and I wouldn't
be afraid to trust her in anything now.

00:22:37.900 --> 00:22:41.610
The first day I saw her three
years ago I was really shocked.

00:22:42.350 --> 00:22:46.490
Lawful heart, shall I
ever forget that tantrum of hers!

00:22:46.640 --> 00:22:51.850
I told my husband, "Marilla Cuthbert'll
live to rue the step she's took."

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:07.480
Honestly, until recently, I was worried
that she wouldn't get rid of her temper.

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:09.680
Marilla,

00:23:10.450 --> 00:23:14.710
I ain't one of those people that can never
admit that they've made a mistake.

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:17.780
That never was my way, thank goodness.

00:23:18.390 --> 00:23:23.190
I did make a mistake in judging
Anne, but it weren't no wonder,

00:23:23.770 --> 00:23:29.300
for I never saw a strange
child like her in my entire life.

00:23:29.900 --> 00:23:34.580
There was no ciphering her out by the rules
that worked with other children.

00:23:35.240 --> 00:23:39.390
It's nothing short of wonderful how
she's improved these three years,

00:23:39.630 --> 00:23:41.570
but especially in looks.

00:23:41.740 --> 00:23:44.380
She's a real pretty girl now.

00:23:54.970 --> 00:23:58.930
Anne doesn't know about Matthew's heart.

00:23:59.030 --> 00:24:03.400
Neither does she know that Marilla
is worried about her health.

00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:08.540
She is just enjoying her vacation.

00:24:17.790 --> 00:24:19.310
The entrance exam is coming

00:24:19.310 --> 00:24:21.950
and the absences from
the Story Club is increasing.

00:24:22.210 --> 00:24:25.100
Next episode of Anne of Green Gables:

00:24:25.220 --> 00:24:27.000
The Future of the Story Club.

00:24:27.140 --> 00:24:28.000
Please watch!
